  "preregistered_hypothesis": "frozen-first (c16/c9, anti-tune-to-green). (A) Ammann-Beenker vertex tight-binding major-gap IDOS plateaus lie in the silver-mean 2D cut-and-project module M_AB = {(a+b*sqrt2)/8 : a,b in Z} (the Z[sqrt2]/8 ring; RANK-2 over Z in basis {1,sqrt2}), fitting it better than a generic rational ladder. (B) M_AB is DISTINCT from any single 1D irrational rotation {n*alpha mod 1} (Fibonacci 1/phi or 1D-silver 1/sqrt2): the rank-2 {1,sqrt2} structure (b!=0 terms) is genuinely needed. (C) CONTROL: a periodic 2D square lattice shows NO such fractal gap ladder. FALSIFIER: gaps don't fit M_AB, or a single 1D rotation suffices (rank-2 unneeded), or the control also shows it -> RED. Under-resolved patch (gaps ~ level spacing) -> honest INCONCLUSIVE.",
