  "finding": "INCONCLUSIVE (honest, c9): the finite Ammann-Beenker patch (953 trimmed vertices) did not resolve clean major gaps clearly above the finite-size mean level spacing (8.830e-03); n_sig=0, min sig gap=0.000e+00. The construction is sound (cut-and-project, mean coordination 3.83) but a larger patch / cleaner window is needed for a definitive 2D module fit. Not forcing a match. Best 2D-module fit so far: 0/0 at max res None. Breakthrough path: grow the 4D box / sharpen the octagon window / use inflation instead of projection.",
  "honest_caveat": "Finite Ammann-Beenker cluster (1737 vertices raw, 953 after boundary trim) under OPEN boundary -- a finite patch, not infinite-volume. IDOS plateau k/N is a rational converging to the true gap label as N->inf (gap-labeling = Bellissard C*-algebra K-theory; for AB the labelled gaps lie in (1/8)Z[sqrt2]). Residuals are O(1/N) + boundary-mode limited; res_tol=0.010 pre-registered (looser than the 1D ring probes because a 2D open cluster has more boundary states). We test module FIT + the DISTINCTION (rank-2 {1,sqrt2} vs single 1D rotation) + a periodic control, not exact equality. The window is the exact unit-4-cube projection (canonical AB octagon), not a tuned size. Boundary (under-coordinated) vertices are trimmed so the bulk gap structure -- the discriminating signal -- dominates over finite-edge artefacts. The full AB gap-label group is rank-2 over Z in {1,sqrt2} (the 8-fold cut-and-project module); we report the dominant low-index labels."
